// Krylov.cgne — single-RHS CGNE (CG on the normal equations of the second kind: solves AAᵀy=b by
// conjugate gradients and forms x=Aᵀy implicitly, matrix-free). For an underdetermined consistent
// system A x = b (A is m×n, m<=n, full row rank) it converges to the minimum-‖x‖ solution
// x* = Aᵀ(AAᵀ)⁻¹b -- the SAME x craig computes, but via a direct CG recurrence on the (never-formed)
// AAᵀ rather than Golub-Kahan bidiagonalization. Because it runs CG directly on AAᵀ, its effective
// conditioning is cond(A)² (vs craig's cond(A)); the diagonally-boosted test matrices below are
// engineered κ≈1 (a +10 boost on random [-1,1] rows), so κ² stays ≈1 and the tolerances match
// craig's -- the κ² sensitivity is exercised where it matters (a genuinely conditioned wide matrix)
// in the battery, KrylovLstsqBatteryTests, not here.
//
// Oracle for the min-norm value: LQ.minNormSolve (exact x* via LQ factorization).
